' ============================================================
' OpenGL 3D - a full 3D renderer for GameBasiX
'
'@help
'# OpenGL 3D
'
'A complete 3D wrapper. On Windows it uses a hidden **OpenGL 1.1** context; in
'the HTML5 player the same commands run through a built-in software
'rasterizer, so one project works in the editor, the EXE and the browser.
'After each frame the pixels are copied into the normal GameBasiX screen, so
'the existing `SCREEN_SHOW`, input and 2D drawing keep working.
'
'The module is the folder `modules/opengl3d`; `OPENGL3D.gbx` is its entry
'file. Add it with the Modules dock or write:
'
'```gbx
'INCLUDE "modules/opengl3d/OPENGL3D.gbx"
'```
'
'## Quick start
'
'```gbx
'INCLUDE "modules/opengl3d/OPENGL3D.gbx"
'
'SCREEN_SET 960, 640, 0
'WINDOW_TITLE "OpenGL 3D"
'ALLOW_ESCAPE FALSE
'GL3D_INIT 960, 640
'
'WHILE TRUE
'  IF KEY_PRESSED(KEY_ESC) THEN END
'
'  GL3D_BEGIN RGB(12, 16, 24)
'  GL3D_PERSPECTIVE 55, 1.5, 0.1, 100
'  GL3D_CAMERA 0, 5, 12, 0, 0, 0
'  GL3D_GRID 20, 1, RGB(40, 50, 62)
'  GL3D_CUBE 0, 1, 0, 1.2, RGB(163, 230, 53), 20, 35, 10
'  GL3D_END
'
'  SCREEN_SHOW
'WEND
'```
'
'## Projections
'
'| Command | Meaning |
'| --- | --- |
'| `GL3D_PERSPECTIVE [fov[, aspect[, near[, far]]]]` | Perspective projection (default 60°, screen aspect, 0.1…100) |
'| `GL3D_ORTHO [left, right, bottom, top[, near[, far]]]]` | Orthographic projection; without arguments the whole screen with y down |
'| `GL3D_CAMERA eyeX, eyeY, eyeZ, targetX, targetY, targetZ` | View matrix, up is +Y |
'
'`GL3D_ORTHO` is meant for HUD panels and 2D overlays inside the 3D frame. It
'resets the camera and draws in screen pixels, so call `GL3D_PERSPECTIVE` and
'`GL3D_CAMERA` again when you want the 3D view back — for example at the start
'of the next frame, because each frame keeps the projection that was used
'last.
'
'## Transform stack
'
'Every primitive is placed by the current model transform. `GL3D_BEGIN` resets
'it at the start of a frame.
'
'| Command | Meaning |
'| --- | --- |
'| `GL3D_IDENTITY` | Resets the model transform |
'| `GL3D_PUSH` / `GL3D_POP` | Saves and restores it (up to 64 levels) |
'| `GL3D_TRANSLATE x, y, z` | Moves the origin |
'| `GL3D_ROTATE degrees[, axisX, axisY, axisZ]` | Rotates around an axis, default +Y |
'| `GL3D_SCALE sx[, sy[, sz]]` | Scales; one argument scales evenly |
'
'```gbx
'GL3D_PUSH
'  GL3D_TRANSLATE 0, 1.4, 0
'  GL3D_ROTATE ELAPSED_TIME() / 12
'  GL3D_CUBE 0, 0, 0, 0.9, RGB(163, 230, 53)
'GL3D_POP
'```
'
'## Render state
'
'| Command | Meaning |
'| --- | --- |
'| `GL3D_DEPTH [enabled]` | Depth test, default on |
'| `GL3D_CULL [enabled]` | Drops back faces; boxes, spheres and cylinders are wound for it |
'| `GL3D_BLEND [enabled]` | Alpha blending, default on |
'| `GL3D_ALPHA alpha` | Alpha for following primitives, 0…1, default 1 |
'| `GL3D_LINE_WIDTH width` | Line and grid width in pixels, 1…32 |
'| `GL3D_POINT_SIZE size` | Dot size for `GL3D_POINT`, 1…64 |
'
'## Lighting
'
'Boxes, cubes, spheres and cylinders are lit by one directional light; lines,
'triangles and quads keep the exact colour you pass.
'
'| Command | Meaning |
'| --- | --- |
'| `GL3D_LIGHT x, y, z` | Direction towards the light (default above, front, right) |
'| `GL3D_AMBIENT value` | Brightness of the unlit side, 0…1, default 0.35 |
'
'Spheres shade smoothly (Gouraud), boxes and cylinders per face.
'
'## Primitives
'
'| Command | Meaning |
'| --- | --- |
'| `GL3D_CUBE x, y, z, size, color[, rotX[, rotY[, rotZ]]]` | Cube; `size` is the half extent |
'| `GL3D_BOX x, y, z, width, height, depth, color[, rotX[, rotY[, rotZ]]]` | Box with full extents |
'| `GL3D_SPHERE x, y, z, radius, color[, segments]` | Sphere with smooth shading |
'| `GL3D_CYLINDER x, y, z, radius, height, color[, segments[, topRadius]]` | Cylinder standing on the point; `topRadius 0` gives a cone |
'| `GL3D_QUAD x1, y1, z1, x2, y2, z2, x3, y3, z3, x4, y4, z4, color` | Flat quad in one colour, unlit |
'| `GL3D_GRID size, step, color` | Grid on the X/Z plane |
'| `GL3D_LINE x1, y1, z1, x2, y2, z2, color` | Single line |
'| `GL3D_TRIANGLE x1, y1, z1, x2, y2, z2, x3, y3, z3, color` | Single filled triangle |
'| `GL3D_POINT x, y, z, color` | Dot, size from `GL3D_POINT_SIZE` |
'| `GL3D_AXIS [length]` | X/Y/Z axes in red, green and blue |
'
'Colours use the normal `RGB()` value; `GL3D_ALPHA` applies on top of it.
'Cube `size` is the half extent, box sizes are full extents.
'
'## Textures
'
'Images that you load with the normal GameBasiX commands (`SPRITE_LOAD`,
'`SPRITE_GRAB`, `ANIM_LOAD`) can be used directly as textures; the renderer
'reads their pixels through the INLINE bridge, so no second loader and no
'extra file format is needed. The HTML5 player works the same way, because
'the sprite is already in memory.
'
'| Command | Meaning |
'| --- | --- |
'| `GL3D_TEXTURE sprite[, smooth]` | Uses a loaded image as texture; `0` clears it, `smooth 1` enables bilinear filtering, returns 1 on success |
'| `GL3D_QUAD_TEX x1, y1, z1, …, x4, y4, z4, color` | Textured quad, unlit |
'| `GL3D_CUBE_TEX x, y, z, size, color[, rotX[, rotY[, rotZ]]]` | Textured cube, lit per face |
'
'```gbx
'GLOBAL crate = 7                       ' sprite numbers are plain integers
'SPRITE_LOAD "assets/crate.png", crate
'GL3D_TEXTURE crate, 1
'GL3D_CUBE_TEX 0, 1, 0, 1.2, RGB(255, 255, 255), 20, 35, 10
'GL3D_TEXTURE 0
'```
'
'The texture stays bound until you change or clear it, so bind it once per
'frame before the textured primitives. `color` works as a tint (multiplied
'with the image), and `GL3D_ALPHA` applies on top. Textured quads and cubes
'only; spheres, cylinders and the line primitives stay untextured. Transparent
'pixels of the image blend when `GL3D_BLEND` is on.
'
'## Frame and queries
'
'| Command | Meaning |
'| --- | --- |
'| `GL3D_INIT [width[, height]]` | Creates the renderer; returns 1 on success |
'| `GL3D_BEGIN [color]` | Starts a frame, clears colour and depth, resets transforms |
'| `GL3D_END` | Finishes the frame and copies it into the GBX screen |
'| `GL3D_INFO$()` | Active backend, for example `OpenGL 1.1` or the software renderer |
'| `GL3D_WIDTH()` / `GL3D_HEIGHT()` | Render resolution |
'| `GL3D_SHUTDOWN` | Releases the OpenGL context |
'
'## Limits
'
'- Windows renders with OpenGL 1.1 immediate mode; no shaders, extensions or
'  extra libraries are needed.
'- The HTML5 player has no OpenGL context, so the module uses a software
'  rasterizer with z-buffer, Gouraud colours, alpha blending and culling.
'- Both paths drop triangles that cross the near plane; keep geometry a little
'  away from the camera.
'- Textures come from images that GameBasiX already loaded; the module has no
'  loader of its own and does not shade them with the directional light
'  (quads) or only per face (cubes).
'- The bridge that hands image pixels to the module needs GameBasiX 1.4 or
'  newer (`GBX_INLINE_VERSION 4`); older builds report a failed
'  `GL3D_TEXTURE`.
'- The INLINE block is compiled on first run and cached like every GBX INLINE
'  block. A C++ compiler must be configured in GBX Studio.
'- The module renders offscreen and copies the result into the current GBX
'  screen; it does not take over the SDL window.
'@endhelp
'
'@tooltip OPENGL3D
'Full 3D wrapper with a perspective or orthographic camera, a transform stack,
'lighting, boxes, spheres, cylinders, grids, lines, triangles, quads and
'points, plus textures from sprites that GameBasiX already loaded. OpenGL on
'Windows, built-in software rasterizer in HTML5.
'@endtooltip

INLINE
#include "opengl3d.h"
ENDINLINE
